# DEFECT 2571, beside it: a trap the library before the runtime declines is
# still told (2026-11-15).
#
# The lease handler now lets a signal go where the handler it found comes
# back having edited the register file. A library declining a trap it did
# not make, as Go's archive declines a fault, puts back the default it found
# and returns with the register file as it was, so the trap would run again
# and the process die of it in silence. The handler reads the file before
# and after the call, finds it as it was, and tells the death as it always
# did. The trap is `__builtin_trap()`: SIGTRAP on arm64 and SIGILL on x86-64
# (`fixedbugs-2571-library.h`).

extern "fixedbugs-2571-library.h"
    function lib_trap_declined()

function main()
    print("before")
    lib_trap_declined()
    print("not reached")
